  data:  # 2eb6
    kind: work_item  # 2eb6
    title: "measure-taint-precision.py prepends its own tree's packages to sys.path, so a PYTHONPATH-selected baseline arm silently measures the script's tree (A/B delta 0 by construction)"  # 2eb6
    status: todo_hard  # 2eb6
    priority: 2  # 2eb6
    parent:  # 2eb6
    tags:  # 2eb6
    - measurement  # 2eb6
    - taint  # 2eb6
    - instrument  # 2eb6
    isbefore: []  # 2eb6
    duplicate_of: []  # 2eb6
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2eb6
    pr_ref:  # 2eb6
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 by WI-valav's taint A/B on pretix (record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/valav/).\n\nWHAT HAPPENS. `scripts/measure-taint-precision.py` lines 97-100 insert `<script's repo>/packages/*/src` at `sys.path[0]`. `sys.path.insert(0, ...)` beats `PYTHONPATH`. So the documented A/B shape -- \"Same instrument, from the working tree, in both arms\", the baseline arm selected by a baseline `PYTHONPATH` (measurement 0003's Method; 0015 reuses it) -- runs the WORKING TREE's analyzer in BOTH arms whenever the script is invoked from the working tree. The run exits 0 and reports plausible numbers.\n\nOBSERVED. Baseline arm: `env PYTHONPATH=<origin/dev export>/packages/*/src python3 ~/hg_wt/valav/scripts/measure-taint-precision.py collect --repo pretix ...` with a fresh XDG_CACHE_HOME. Its cached survey's python pass reported `edges_emitted: 113485`. That is the SUBJECT tree's count: `analyze_python` imported from the baseline export gives 113421, and from the subject gives 113485. The baseline and subject surveys had identical call-edge multisets (0 / 0 difference), so the \"delta\" was 0 by construction.\n\nNOT CHECKED. Whether any committed measurement record (0003, 0013-0016, 0021, ...) was affected. 0003's text says the control was verified (\"Under the baseline PYTHONPATH the interpreter resolves taint.py to the clone\"). That check may predate the sys.path pin (bf92fb08cf introduced the script; I did not bisect the pin), or the arm may have run the clone's copy of the script. Each record's arm commands need to be read before saying either way.\n\nWORKAROUND USED. Run each arm with the script copy that lives in that arm's tree (`<base export>/scripts/measure-taint-precision.py`, plus the claims file under `<base export>/docs/example-claims/`). Then the pin selects that arm's code. The control: the python pass's `edges_emitted` in each arm's cached survey.json.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (not built). EITHER let an explicit PYTHONPATH win (append the pin instead of prepending it, or skip it when hypergumbo_core already resolves) OR print the resolved `hypergumbo_core` / `hypergumbo_lang_mainstream` file paths as the first line of `collect`, the way the instrument already prints its positive control. The second keeps the self-locating behaviour and makes the wrong-tree case visible."  # 2eb6
    fields: {}  # 2eb6
- op: discuss  # 5cd7
