    title: "measurement scripts can put their own tree ahead of PYTHONPATH: measure-taint-precision.py from a worktree copy or without the editable install; measure-narrowing-headroom.py and measure-catalogue-exposure.py always (core only, mixed tree)"  # c341
- op: discuss  # 4ab4
  at: '2026-10-03T06:41:59Z'  # 4ab4
  by: agent  # 4ab4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ab4
  clock: 4  # 4ab4
  nonce: 4ab4  # 4ab4
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). Defect real; TRIGGER CONDITION was wrong; scope widened. Title updated.\n- scripts/measure-taint-precision.py:97-100 inserts its own tree's packages, guarded by `if str(_pkg) not in sys.path`. The main .venv's editable-install .pth files already put the main checkout's packages/*/src on sys.path (after PYTHONPATH), so the main-tree script under the main venv inserts NOTHING and PYTHONPATH decides.\n- Repro (fake hypergumbo_core on PYTHONPATH): main-tree script + .venv/bin/python resolves the fake (no trap); a copy of the script in a tree with its own packages/ (a worktree) resolves that copy's tree (trap fires); main-tree script + /usr/bin/python3 without the editable install resolves the main tree (trap fires). So the trap fires for a worktree/clone copy of the script (the valav case) or an interpreter without the editable install, not \"whenever invoked from the working tree\".\n- WORSE SIBLINGS: scripts/measure-narrowing-headroom.py:72 and scripts/measure-catalogue-exposure.py:68 insert core's src at position 0 UNGUARDED. Both resolved the main tree even with PYTHONPATH set to the fake, and they pin only hypergumbo-core, so a PYTHONPATH arm gets a mixed tree (core from the script's tree, language packages from elsewhere). The measure-*-ab.py scripts run both arms in one process and are unaffected.\n- RECORDS AUDIT (the 10-02 triage asked for it): no committed record is demonstrably affected. 0003 and INV-fubag's 08-21 A/B: deltas carry the change's signature (35 added / 0 removed; 29 removed / 6 kept), which identical arms cannot produce. 0013/0014/0015/0016/0021: arms checked out in place, no PYTHONPATH. 0029: console-script entry, the insertion never runs. mojaz_remeasure: single arm. valav first baseline: affected, already discarded (taint_base_INVALID_ran_subject_code/). rovun: used the workaround. \"0015 reuses it\" referred to 0003's delta-census question, not this mechanism.\n- The suggested fix (print the resolved module paths) fits all three scripts."  # 4ab4
- op: discuss  # 61dc
  at: '2026-10-03T08:04:35Z'  # 61dc
  by: agent  # 61dc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 61dc
  clock: 5  # 61dc
  nonce: 61dc  # 61dc
  message: "FIX BUILT 2026-10-03 (decontend run_10032026, stage 1). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/tumog, commit 564e2dcdec (local, not pushed). Status NOT changed.\n\nWHAT. New scripts/measure_code_tree.py (stdlib only), wired into measure-taint-precision.py (collect AND packet), measure-narrowing-headroom.py and measure-catalogue-exposure.py.\n- pin(): if PYTHONPATH supplies an in-scope package (hypergumbo_core; for the taint script also every hypergumbo_lang_*) from a directory other than the script's own tree, the script REFUSES with exit 2, names both, and asks for HG_MEASURE_TREE=script or HG_MEASURE_TREE=pythonpath. No conflict: the script's tree is pinned first, as before. An unknown HG_MEASURE_TREE value: exit 2.\n- announce(): before any output, prints \"code under test: <tree>\" plus each package's directory, says when that is NOT the script's tree and who chose it, and refuses a MIXED tree (in-scope packages resolving to more than one tree).\n- measure-catalogue-exposure.py: catalogue_dir() now reads io_boundary._CATALOG_DIR from the IMPORTED core; it used to read the language list from beside the script (a second mixed-tree route).\n- docs/measurements/README.md: new section \"Which tree an arm measures\".\n\nWHY REFUSE INSTEAD OF \"PYTHONPATH WINS\". The board pins PYTHONPATH to the worktree it runs in, so \"PYTHONPATH wins\" would make a baseline copy of the script, run under slot from the subject worktree, measure the subject: the same silent wrong arm, reversed. Each precedence order is right for one documented workflow and wrong for the other, so a disagreement is refused and the caller chooses.\n\nBEHAVIOUR CHANGE TO NOTE FOR LATER STAGES. The AGENT_PROMPT A/B recipe (run the baseline arm with the baseline export's copy of the script) now exits 2 under `slot run` (PYTHONPATH pinned to the worktree) until HG_MEASURE_TREE=script is set. A lone copy of the NEW script without scripts/measure_code_tree.py beside it fails with ModuleNotFoundError (rc 1).\n\nEVIDENCE (behavioural, through the board). Fake hypergumbo_core / hypergumbo_lang_* packages on PYTHONPATH that print FAKE-TREE-IMPORTED and exit 97 on import. Red run before the fix: 15 failed, 76 passed, 3 errors (helper absent); each script exited 0 having run the script's tree (taint collect and packet rc 0 with the fake on PYTHONPATH; exposure printed its table; narrowing printed its report). After: smart-test targeted run 531 passed + 1 failed (test_no_declared_glob_has_rotted, because the new helper was still untracked); after committing, 474 passed, 0 failed (24 files, incl. test_measure_code_tree 20, test_measure_taint_precision 13, test_measure_catalogue_exposure 17, test_measure_narrowing_headroom 4, test_adjudication_packet 76, test_top_level_test_map 46). mypy strict ratchet clean.\nLive repro of the WI-valav shape: worktree copy of measure-taint-precision.py, PYTHONPATH = the main checkout's packages/*/src:\n  unset -> rc 2, \"WHICH CODE IS MEASURED IS AMBIGUOUS\", names /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/hypergumbo-core/src\n  HG_MEASURE_TREE=pythonpath -> rc 0, \"code under test: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo (NOT this script's tree ...)\"; independent control: the run's UserWarning came from /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/.../cli.py\n  HG_MEASURE_TREE=script (fresh XDG cache) -> rc 0, \"code under test: /home/jgstern_agent/hg_wt/tumog (this script's tree ...)\"; warning from /home/jgstern_agent/hg_wt/tumog/.../cli.py\n\nSWEEP of scripts/ by mechanism (grep sys.path.insert; sys.path.append / [:0] / addsitedir: none):\n- FIXED: measure-taint-precision.py, measure-narrowing-headroom.py, measure-catalogue-exposure.py.\n- NOT CHANGED, own tree pinned first and only that tree's core imported at the script level (gates and generators that read or write their own tree; a PYTHONPATH arm is not a use-case, and their precedence keeps code and files from one tree): check-audit-findings, check-docstring-drift, check-edge-type-drift, check-edge-type-runtime-coherence, check-evidence-type-drift, check-fallback-coherence, check-io-boundary-drift, check-meta-write-discipline, check-producer-axis-coherence, check-schema-coverage, check-symbol-kind-drift, check-test-only-reachability, compute_probe_embeddings.py, coverage-select, generate-architecture, generate-catalogues-doc, generate-concept-axes, yaml-catalog-index. Transitive imports inside the core modules they call were NOT audited.\n- NOT CHANGED, pins EVERY packages/*/src of its own tree (self-consistent gate): check-pass-id-agreement, check-id-construction, check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration, check-recorded-producer-input.\n- NOT the mechanism (insert scripts/lib for pool_utils, no hypergumbo package): bakeoff-broad, bakeoff-broad-reflect, bakeoff-deep, bakeoff-deep-reflect, dead-code-prospector-run.py.\n- RESIDUAL, filed as WI-sotih-lupug-zupup-majus-panom-dafom-dajan-piguk (P3): generate-schema's pin names REPO_ROOT/src, which does not exist, so it imports core from PYTHONPATH or the editable install and writes REPO_ROOT/docs/schema.json; regenerate-backend-agreement-table pins no package and writes docs/audits/0019. Both pair the script's tree's files with another tree's code when run from a worktree without PYTHONPATH.\n- NOT CHECKED: measure-*-ab.py and the other measure-*.py scripts that do not insert into sys.path; they import whatever the interpreter resolves (the audit note says the -ab scripts run both arms in one process)."  # 61dc
