- op: discuss  # cba1
  at: '2026-10-03T09:40:25Z'  # cba1
  by: agent  # cba1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cba1
  clock: 7  # cba1
  nonce: cba1  # cba1
  message: "Fixed in PR #1408. measure-taint-precision.py (`collect` and `packet`), measure-narrowing-headroom.py and measure-catalogue-exposure.py now call scripts/measure_code_tree.py:\n- When PYTHONPATH supplies hypergumbo_core (or, for the taint script, a hypergumbo_lang_* package) from a directory other than the script's tree, they exit 2 and name both, unless HG_MEASURE_TREE=script|pythonpath chooses.\n- Every run prints `code under test: <tree>` and each package directory before any number, and refuses a mixed tree.\n- Exposure's language list now comes from the imported core.\n\nBehavioural evidence: fake hypergumbo_core / hypergumbo_lang_* on PYTHONPATH (exit 97 on import).\n- Before the fix, 15 tests failed with each script exiting 0 having run its own tree.\n- After the fix: 474 passed, 0 failed.\n\nLive repro of the WI-valav shape (worktree copy, PYTHONPATH = main checkout):\n- unset: rc 2.\n- `pythonpath`: rc 0, provenance and cli.py warnings both from /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo.\n- `script`: rc 0, both from hg_wt/tumog.\n\nThe general claim \"no script can measure the wrong tree\" is NOT asserted. generate-schema and regenerate-backend-agreement-table are filed as WI-sotih, and scripts that never pin a tree were not changed."  # cba1
